Hi,

Thanks to Andrew Wagg, Elin Vaeth, Peter Wolfe and Dr Thomas Blinn for =
pointing out that dxprint(1X) is in the list of retired DECwindows =
applications in Section 2.1.1 of the Tru64 V5.1 release notes lists :

http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V51_HTML/ARH8WBTE/T=
ITLE.HTM

This retirement has been advertised in the release notes since about =
v4.0f (section 8.1).=20
There is no longer any direct equivalent for dxprint under Tru64 5.X .

Now I need to look at the suggested alternatives, mainly the use of xwd, =
xpr, and the dtlp command which is suggested by earlier release notes

http://discovery.cc.vt.edu/dec/AQTLMCTE/DOCU_009.HTM

Andrew has made used of the free set of tools =
http://www.imagemagick.org/ to achieve a similar result as dxprint.
He wrapped them in a tcl/tk wish script in order to provide a similair =
looking interface.=20
For black & white prints he made use of xwd to capture the screen and =
xpr to print it, which is what most others have suggested.

Best regards,
Michael



