Hi all,

please does anybody know if the 5.1A takes into account the kernel =
parameter vm-swap-eager or vm_swap_eager ?=20

"man swapon" tells vm-swap-eager (see =
http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V51A_HTML/MAN/MAN8/=
0405____.HTM)

The System Configuration and Tuning Manual tells vm_swap_eager (see =
http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V51A_PDF/ARH9GBTE.P=
DF)

I can ask both of them:
     =20
alpha99# sysconfig -q vm vm_swap_eager
vm:
vm_swap_eager =3D 1
alpha99# sysconfig -q vm vm-swap-eager
vm:
vm-swap-eager =3D 1

The original sysconfig database seems to have only one:
alpha99# sysconfig -q vm | grep eager       =20
vm_swap_eager =3D 1

But if I set vm-swap-eager according the "man swapon", I can see it in =
the sysconfigtab:
alpha99# grep eager sysconfigtab
vm_swap_eager =3D 0
vm-swap-eager =3D 1


Which one has the higher priority?

With Regards,

Martin
