Thanks to Tom Blinn, Lucio Chiappetti, and Phil Baldwin for replying and
pointing me in the right direction.

After reading everyone's replies it became apparent the problem was a host
resolution problem, not a mail problem.  We had an unusual entry in the
/etc/resolv.conf file for the domain.  We also decided to setup DNS on this
box.  The DNS setup changed the domain entry in the resolv.conf file to the
valid domain.  Mail is now working!

