Hi all,

because many of you answered even after I had sent my first summary, =
thanks again and especially to M.R.Andersen who provided a link to the =
source of the documentation.

The correct syntax is really vm_swap_eager since 5.0, but the old shape =
with dashes does work as well,
see the "Tru64 UNIX Release Notes for 5.0, Part Number AA-RH8WA-TE, July =
1999", =
http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V50_PDF/ARH8WATE.PD=
F :
"1.10.5    Kernel Attribute Changes
All kernel attribute names now use underscores. They no longer contain =
dashes. Old kernel attribute names using dashes are hidden; they are no =
longer automatically shown in the output of a query operation. Although =
existing tools and programs using the old attribute names still work in =
this release, the old names with dashes will be retired in a future =
release. For more information on kernel attributes, see the sys_attrs(5) =
reference page."


I believe, that because Release Notes for 5.0A, 5.1, 5.1A nor 5.1B don't =
mention the dashes to be retired in "this" release and 5.1B should be =
the last v5 for ever, the Tru64 v5 could live with dashes until it dies =
(the next Tru64 will have version 11i v3).

With Best Regards,

Martin

