makes it=20
>appear to be a CRC and/or Frame error).  In general, Ethernet is a =
datagram=20
>medium, and no datagram transmit is ever guaranteed to make it to the =
destination.=20
>
>Store-forward mode is never an issue in 10mb mode but it is in 100mb. =
Store-forward=20
>mode insures that the entire packet is in the chip  BEFORE the transmit =
starts=20
>because some systems cannot DMA data fast enough to the chip in 100mb =
mode.
>=20
>Basically, the system cannot keep up with the chip. The customer needs =
to run=20
>with store-forward enabled to avoid the  fifo underflow.=20
>
>To enable store-forward mode when the tu driver starts,=20
>patch the variable "tu_sf_mode" using dbx.
>
>EX:
>=3D=3D=3D=3D
>
># dbx -k  /vmunix =20
>
>(dbx) print tu_sf_mode=20
>0
>
>(dbx) patch tu_sf_mode=3D1=20
>1 =20
>
>(dbx) print tu_sf_mode=20
>1
>
>(dbx) quit
>
>**************
>=20
>You may want/need to restart the network (#/usr/sbin/rcinet restart)=20

To survive a reboot, use the dbx 'assign' command rather than 'patch'

There is also the option of changing to use DE60x interface instead of =
the DE50x.
The DE60x does not suffer from the buffering problems caused by the =
delay_6694F patch.




