Hi,

yes i just configured LAG on a v5.1A system=
.

I did the following:
- normal network configuration for the first =
interface ee0
- added the following lines to /etc/inet.local
echo "/et=
c/inet.local: configuring link aggregation:"
ifconfig ee0 down
ifconfi=
g ee0 delete
lagconfig -c lag=3Dlag0
lagconfig -p ee0 key=3D1
lagconf=
ig -p ee1 key=3D1
ifconfig lag0 $IFCONFIG_0 up
echo ""

I think, Net=
rain and LAG cannot coexist on the same =

interfaces.

It is important, that there is a network config for one 
interface
in /etc/rc.config. Before i did this, the default route was 
lost.
