Hi all,

V5.1B PK2

I'm in the process of replacing 2 failing SCSI disks.

I unplugged them (dsk40 and 41) and ran 'hwmgr -scan scsi' and noted that
the two drives were no longer shown on that scsi bus.
I plugged in the 2 new drives and again ran 'hwmgr -scan scsi'
and noted the arrival of 2 new drives (dsk99 and 100) on that bus.

I want to use the old dsk numbers for the new drives, so I then did

hwmgr delete -id 155   (155 was the hwid of the old dsk40)

followed by

dsfmgr -m dsk99 dsk44

So far, so good.

I then tried to delete the entry for dsk41

hwmgr delete -id 156   (156 is the hwid of the old dsk41)

and got:

hwmgr: Error (95) Cannot start operation.

I then (successfully) used

dsfmgr -e dsk41 dsk100

to swap the device ids, and again tried to delete the hwid entry
(now for dsk100)

hwmgr delete -id 156

again got:
hwmgr: Error (95) Cannot start operation.


I get the same error if I use the deviceid instead of the hwid

hwmgr delete -did 41


Any ideas?


Terry.


